# UI design

## Typography

- Do **not** use italic / cursive display greetings like “Hello, Name” or “Epic work, Name” in a script/serif italic voice — that reads as AI slop.
- Prefer clean sans UI type; expressive serif only when the product already uses it for a specific non-greeting role, and never italicized name greetings.

## Buttons (Miro-like)

- Buttons, chips, inputs, selects, segmented controls, **tabs**, **filter Apply / preset chrome**, zoom chrome, and slide-nav actions use **soft rects**: `rounded-md` (not pills, not `rounded-lg` / `rounded-2xl` on the control itself).
- Do **not** use `rounded-full` on buttons/CTAs/triggers/toolbars. Keep `rounded-full` only for true circles (avatars, switches, color dots, tiny status badges, regulation-pad pucks).
- Editor tabs / intensity segments: `rounded-md` list shell + `rounded-md` triggers (`sidebarTabs*` / `sidebarSegmented*`).

## Select + Tabs

- Prefer **shadcn** `Select` over native `<select>`. Sidebar: `sidebarSelectTrigger`.
- Control height: change once in `components/ui/control.ts` (`controlH`, currently `h-11`). Do not restate `h-*` on Button/Input/SelectTrigger; raw shells use `cn(..., controlH)`.
- Select trigger: `rounded-md`, height from `controlH`, `bg-muted/40`, `px-3.5`, `text-[13px] font-normal`, no border/shadow.
- Select item: `rounded-md`, `py-2.5`, generous horizontal padding, `font-normal`, `focus:bg-muted/50`.
- Tabs list + trigger: both `rounded-md`; trigger `px-3`, `font-normal`; active = `bg-background` (no `ring-*`).
- Do **not** use `rounded-full` or heavy `font-medium` on Select/Tabs labels.

## Surfaces

- Use borders sparingly. Prefer spacing, typography, and background contrast over `border` outlines.
- Buttons / chips / dialogs: no box shadows. Dropdown / select / popover panels: `shadow-sm` + `border-0` (`bg-popover`); in dark also `border-border/50`. Dialogs: `border-border/50` + `shadow-none` (`bg-background`).

## Themes

- Every UI change must work in **light and dark** via Tailwind (`dark:` variants, semantic tokens like `bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `muted-foreground`).

## Components

- Prefer **shadcn** primitives from `@/components/ui/*` (Button, Dialog, DropdownMenu, Input, etc.) before custom one-offs.
- Extend shadcn with `className` / variants; don’t reinvent the same controls.

## Left sidebar spacing

- Every left-sidebar panel root uses the shared `sidebarPanel` class from `sidebar-ui.ts` (`px-3.5 py-3 gap-3`). Settings included. Don’t invent per-panel padding.

## Icons (studio + editor)

- Product icons match Miro density: **`size-5 stroke-[1.5]`** (`navIconClass` / `menuIconClass`).
- Tiny chevrons / status glyphs may stay `size-3`–`size-3.5`. Do not mix `size-4` as the default.

## Filters over chrome (Figma density)

Maximize canvas/sidebar space. Do **not** park permanent chip rows, category tabs, tag strips, source pills, or variant switchers in the main chrome.

- Lists / categories / tags / sources / scopes / sorts → one compact **filter button** (icon `ListFilter`) opening a menu (`FilterMenu` or equivalent). Search may sit beside it.
- Default view shows content only. Active filter is indicated on the button (muted fill / check in menu), not by a second always-visible chip bar.
- Don’t stamp tags/categories on every tile in the grid; keep taxonomy in the filter (and detail/edit when needed).
- Exception: a control that **is** the primary task (e.g. typing a color, editing SVG) — not browse taxonomy.
